00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.139 align:start position:0%
 
Wow  can you get a business loan if you don't  have revenue it's a question that came  in from mo who's one of my youtube  viewers most amazing has a great smile  ask the ton of questions is always  active so thank you mo and i love to  answer this question for you here's the  thing banks are typically not the best  place to go to for funding your business  because banks do not take risk they want  to make sure that they're going to get  their money back so if you're just  starting up the bank is not the place to  go if you want to get a small business  loan then absolutely they want to see  revenue growth not just revenue they  want to see profits if you have revenue  but you're losing money it's going to be  really hard to get a bank loan they want  to see three years of traction and  growth so you're gonna have to show the  last three years of your top line  revenue and your bottom line profits and  it better be growing and it better look  good or they're not going to say yes  just my business loan because it's risky  because most businesses fail and they  don't want to be attached to that they  want to get their money back they want  to be able to grab on to something in  case it doesn't work out so typically  the only way to get a small business  loan as a start-up is to have a personal  guarantee so that means if you can't pay  the loan back from your business you are  on the hook personally they can take  your car they could take your house they  could take any investments that you have  you are personally on the hook for  repaying that loan if you really need to  get money then as a start-up the best  places to get it first of all is  bootstrap don't spend money I hate  spending money till I'm making money try  to find a way to get it from your  customers put that money back into your  business it's slower growth but you're  going to be able to make and build a  more successful business because you  know what you're doing you're building  and you're learning the process as you  go through if that's not working out  fast enough for you then your next best  bet is to look at friends and family  look at people who you know who might be  able to invest in your business and  often the people who do it aren't the  people who are closest to you they're  not your uncle or your aunt or your  parents or your brothers and sisters  it's the people who are in a much wider  network maybe  somebody went to high school with so you  got to spread the word beyond your  immediate network if you need to go get  that loan be prepared to give that  personal guarantee or they're not going  to say yes to you but again I hate  spending money until I'm making money so  go find a way to hustle bootstrap get  something of value that you can sell to  your customers get money in the door  start building that business up and then  when you're ready to expand then it's  easy to go after a banker or an angel  investor or even a venture capitalist if  you have bigger dreams because you've  shown that it can work on a small scale  I know you're really ready to ramp up  thanks for the question mo believe for  those of you watching you like the video  please give it a thumbs up below makes  me want to do more for you and I'd love  to hear your questions and your comments  below i'll make a video reply for people  who write in thank you guys i'll see you  soon

